Sval: Sval is its own vendor, with its own profile directory, and Firefox's user agent

MOZ_APP_VENDOR, MOZ_APP_PROFILE and MOZ_APP_UA_NAME are project flags, which
only an imply_option in a Mozilla .configure file can set, so no mozconfig
or branding option reaches them. All three are compiled into libxul in a
full build. The vendor names the Windows registry keys and %APPDATA%
directory Sval uses, and the profile names its profile directory on every
platform: ~/Library/Application Support/Sval, %APPDATA%\Sval and ~/.sval.
Without this, a full Sval build shares Firefox's.

MOZ_APP_UA_NAME is the application name in the user agent. Left empty,
nsHttpHandler falls back to the application's own name, Sval, and writes
"sval/<version>" where Firefox writes "Firefox/<version>". Sval sends
Firefox's user agent, as other Firefox forks do, so sites that recognise
Firefox treat Sval the same.

diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
index 3ea3d88b93..d61496ed37 100644
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -11,7 +11,9 @@ imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 
-imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Mozilla")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Sval")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_PROFILE", "Sval")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_UA_NAME", "Firefox")
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
